# vibe-backup.env.tmpl — rendered to /opt/vibe/env/vibe-backup.env by
# lib/enable-app.sh.
#
# Vibe Backup is the suite's backup-and-verified-restore sidecar:
# nightly restic to a firm-owned Backblaze B2 bucket with Object Lock,
# monthly restore drills with decrypt canaries, and a printed Recovery
# Kit that gates activation. Its ONE way in is the console's
# authenticated proxy (Apps → Vibe Backup card → its link); it has no
# login of its own and no Caddy route, by design.
#
# NO SECRETS IN THIS FILE. The B2 credentials are collected once by the
# app's own setup wizard (the master key is used to provision and never
# stored; the derived restricted keys live in the app's state dir under
# /opt/vibe/data/apps/vibe-backup/state, owned by its non-root uid).
# Everything here is plumbing the appliance decides, not the operator —
# which is why nothing below is surfaced on the Settings page.

# --- Docker access ----------------------------------------------------
# The filtered socket proxy (apps/vibe-backup.yml), never the raw
# socket. Endpoint allowlist: docs/socket-proxy.md in the Vibe-Backup
# repo. If you are debugging "cannot reach Docker", check that the
# vibe-backup-socket-proxy container is running and that both it and
# vibe-backup are on the vibe_backup_socket network.
DOCKER_HOST=tcp://vibe-backup-socket-proxy:2375

# --- The database it protects ----------------------------------------
# Dumps and restores exec INSIDE this container, so client tooling
# always matches the server version and no Postgres credentials are
# needed here.
VIBE_BACKUP_PG_CONTAINER=vibe-postgres

# --- Non-module state captured every night ---------------------------
# Paths inside the sidecar's read-only /host/vibe mount. state.json is
# the appliance's install state (which apps are enabled, config mode).
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: /host/vibe/env and /host/vibe/data/caddy. Those
# trees are root-600 and the sidecar is non-root by upstream policy
# (BK-1), so listing them would fail every backup with EACCES. Per-app
# key material travels the designed channel instead — each app's
# .vibe-backup module contract (Vibe-Backup phase BK-2b) reads secrets
# via container inspect. Until the env/caddy question is settled with
# the Vibe-Backup repo, keep Duplicati's whole-tree backup configured.
VIBE_BACKUP_EXTRA_PATHS=/host/vibe/state.json

# --- Appliance-mode discovery cross-check ----------------------------
# DELIBERATELY UNSET: VIBE_BACKUP_APPLIANCE_MANIFEST expects a
# {"modules":[{"slug":...}]} document, which this appliance does not
# emit (state.json has a different shape). With it unset the sidecar
# uses label discovery alone — correct today, since no Vibe app ships a
# backup contract yet. Wire it up when BK-2b lands, so a module that is
# installed but missing its contract fails the backup loudly instead of
# being silently excluded.

# --- Optional knobs, copy-paste only ---------------------------------
# Not surfaced in Settings; add below and `sudo docker restart
# vibe-backup`. Preserved across re-renders because this template does
# not name them:
#
#   VIBE_BACKUP_TZ            IANA zone for the 01:30 nightly window
#                             (unset = container-local time, UTC).
#   VIBE_BACKUP_LOCAL_REPO    local restic repo path (USB/NAS mount that
#                             you have ALSO bind-mounted into the
#                             container via an apps/vibe-backup
#                             override). Unset = B2 only; the app warns
#                             but proceeds.
#   VIBE_BACKUP_PING_URL      dead-man's-switch URL, GET after every
#                             successful backup. Any healthchecks-style
#                             endpoint works (docs/deadman-endpoint.md).
#   VIBE_BACKUP_SMTP_HOST / _PORT / _USER / _PASS / _FROM
#                             failure-alert email relay. Unset = alerts
#                             are console-card only. The alert ADDRESS
#                             is collected by the app's own wizard; this
#                             is just the relay it sends through.
